Z||000003||GT Bastard||03-25-2000||09:41 PM||||I'm working on a Supercharger/twin-turbo setup using a weed-wacker motor to replace the A/C. 30 pounds of boost will be fed via twin turbo's in the weed-wacker, which should drop a bone-stock V6 into 8 second 1/4 mile times. The whole kit should cost an estimated $50 dollars.  My ass-o-meter has dyno'd this setup at 900hp and 590lbs of torque. Let me know if you're interested!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||BBBAD GT||03-25-2000||09:52 PM||||What kind of blower is that Rotex? Centrifugal or positive displacement type?  I've never heard of them.  10lb of boost is a lot, and can waste head gaskets or hole a piston easily if its not tuned right.  Do your homework before purchasing, I did before I got mine.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||03-25-2000||09:57 PM||||only 590 ft lbs of torque?<P>can you upgrade to a moped motor instead of the weed wacker.......<P>or a twin weed wacker setup||||reg||1
Z||000006||Superfiero||03-25-2000||10:05 PM||||I dont know if GT Bastard knows anything about forced induction.  Currently I have a Jackson Racing Supercharger on my 95 Acura Integra GSR running 10 pounds and my car runs a 13.4.  I keep on breaking CV joints and it is too expensive to be replacing parts on imports so I'm now in the process of searching for the right V6 to be my next toy.  I don't believe running 13's with a rotrex supercharger is impossible.  If I can pull around 170 naturally aspirated horses out of this 2.8 I don't see why I can't run 13's with an additional 10 psi. Keep in mind my Integra is front wheel drive and the Fiero is rear wheel drive with a lot of weight sitting on the rear wheels.  So if you think this is impossible I would like to hear why.  10 pounds is not a small 50 shot of nitrous, 1 pound of boost is equivalent to 10 horsepower so at 10 pounds that equals an additional 100 horsepower if you cant do the math||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||03-25-2000||10:13 PM||||Isn't the Rotrex a centrifical  design with a cone shaped rotor?<BR>They're the best in Swiss design,after chocolate anyways.||||reg||1
